    "faq": {
      "type": "section-accordion-group",
      "blocks": {
        "q_used_for": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "default_open": false,
            "title": "What is a Kansa Scalp Comb?",
            "content": "<p>A Kansa Scalp Comb is a handcrafted scalp massage tool made from traditional Kansa metal - a blend of copper and tin that has been used in India for centuries in wellness rituals. Think of it as a gua sha for your scalp - designed to gently massage the scalp, support a healthy scalp environment and elevate your daily haircare ritual </p>",
            "show_icon": false,
            "icon_name": "icon-award",
            "icon_size": 20,
            "icon_color": ""
          }
        },
        "q_how_use": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "default_open": false,
            "title": "What is Kansa metal made from?",
            "content": "<p>Traditional Kansa is a blend of 80% copper and 20% tin. This alloy has been used in India for centuries to create wellness tools and is valued for its durability, smooth finish and connection to traditional self-care practices. </p>",
            "show_icon": false,
            "icon_name": "icon-award",
            "icon_size": 20,
            "icon_color": ""
          }
        },
        "q_how_often": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "default_open": false,
            "title": "Can I use the Kansa Scalp Comb every day?",
            "content": "<p>Yes. The Kansa Scalp Comb is gentle enough for daily use. Enjoy a few minutes of scalp massage each day or incorporate it into your weekly hair oiling ritual with the SEVA Hair Strengthening Oil. Use circular motions across the crown, temples and base of the scalp - areas traditionally associated with marma (vital energy) points - to help release built-up tension and encourage relaxation.</p>",
            "show_icon": false,
            "icon_name": "icon-award",
            "icon_size": 20,
            "icon_color": ""
          }
        },
        "q_how_long": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "default_open": false,
            "title": "How do I clean my Kansa Scalp Comb?",
            "content": "<p>Wipe the comb clean after each use. If you've used it with hair oil, wash it gently with mild soap and warm water, then dry it thoroughly before storing</p>",
            "show_icon": false,
            "icon_name": "icon-award",
            "icon_size": 20,
            "icon_color": ""
          }
        },
        "q_treated": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "default_open": false,
            "title": "Why is every SEVA Kansa Scalp Comb unique?",
            "content": "<p>Each comb is individually handcrafted in India by skilled artisans using traditional metalworking techniques passed down through generations. Because every piece is shaped, polished and finished by hand, no two combs are exactly alike.<strong> </strong></p>",
            "show_icon": false,
            "icon_name": "icon-award",
            "icon_size": 20,
            "icon_color": ""
          }
        }
      },
